-- title:
--   Level-one supersingular Hecke entry counts ℓ-isogeny kernels
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, let $q'$ be a prime such that $\kappa$ has characteristic $q'$ and is an algebraic $\mathbb{Z}/q'$-algebra, and let $\ell$ be a nonzero natural number which is prime and distinct from $q'$. Assume the two $\kappa$-algebra maps from the level-one modular function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ 1 = \kappa(j_q, j_{q^1})$ into the degeneracy roof $\mathtt{charLDegeneracyRoof}\ \kappa\ 1\ \ell$, namely the inclusion `heckeAlphaC` and the map `heckeBetaC` induced by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ on Laurent series, are integral ring maps (hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$); the roof is the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by $j_q$, $j_{q^1}$, $j_{q^{\ell}}$ and $j_{q^{1\cdot\ell}}$. Let $x$ and $y$ be places of the level-one modular function field lying in $\mathtt{ssPlaces}\ q'\ 1\ \kappa$, i.e. satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace` for $q'$, and let $E_x, E_y$ be elliptic Weierstrass curves over $\kappa$ whose $j$-invariants are the values at $x$, respectively $y$, of the generator $\mathtt{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ 1 = j_q$, evaluation at a place meaning the preimage in $\kappa$ of the residue of the element when it lies in the valuation subring and $0$ otherwise. Then the $(y,x)$ entry of the supersingular Hecke matrix $\mathtt{ssHeckeMatrixC}\ q'\ \kappa\ 1\ \ell\ h\alpha\ h\beta$ — the finite sum, over those places $W$ of the roof whose restriction along `heckeBetaC` is $x$ and whose restriction along `heckeAlphaC` is $y$, of the ramification index of $W$ along `heckeBetaC` times its inertia degree along `heckeAlphaC` — equals, as an integer, the number of subgroups $C$ of the group of affine points of the base change of $E_x$ to $\kappa$ such that $C$ has cardinality $\ell$ and there exist $\psi$ in $\mathtt{rationalHomSet}\ \kappa\ E_x\ E_y$ and $\psi'$ in $\mathtt{rationalHomSet}\ \kappa\ E_y\ E_x$ (additive point homomorphisms that are either zero or rationally represented) with $\ker \psi = C$, $\psi' \circ \psi = \ell \cdot \mathrm{id}$ and $\psi \circ \psi' = \ell \cdot \mathrm{id}$.
--
--   This is the curve-side computation of the level-one supersingular Hecke matrix: the geometric count of places of the degeneracy roof above a pair of supersingular points is identified with the number of order-$\ell$ subgroups of the column curve that arise as kernels of $\ell$-isogenies onto the row curve, the shape in which Eichler's Brandt matrices present the Hecke action on supersingular points. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_one_kernelIdealSet_of_rationalEndSubring`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_classSet_equiv_ssPlaces_one_kernelIdealSet_of_rationalEndSubring), to match supersingular places with ideal classes of a maximal order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified at $q'$ and infinity.
